prerequisites and permissions.

336
00:23:12.790 --> 00:23:14.540
Intune coexistence.

337
00:23:14.540 --> 00:23:16.902
Intune owns device certificates.

338
00:23:16.902 --> 00:23:21.371
Cloud PKI issues to Intune-managed
devices through SCEP,

339
00:23:21.371 --> 00:23:23.939
and Intune's profiles renew them.

340
00:23:23.939 --> 00:23:25.978
The platform's role there is narrow.

341
00:23:25.978 --> 00:23:27.560
During the bridge period,

342
00:23:27.560 --> 00:23:31.928
some Intune certificates still come
from AD CS through the connector.

343
00:23:31.928 --> 00:23:35.907
Because a Microsoft CA import
brings in mobile, user and client

344
00:23:35.907 --> 00:23:40.728
certificates the platform didn't enroll,
those will appear in its inventory.

345
00:23:40.728 --> 00:23:44.317
The program's guidance is to
import them as monitor-only,

346
00:23:44.317 --> 00:23:48.140
with no renewal binding, so
Intune stays the renewal engine.

347
00:23:48.140 --> 00:23:51.702
There's an option CyberArk
documents that the program rejects.

348
00:23:51.702 --> 00:23:56.785
The platform can act as an Intune
third-party SCEP CA: Intune profiles point at

349
00:23:56.785 --> 00:24:02.027
its SCEP endpoint, and it validates
challenges with Intune through an Entra app.

350
00:24:02.027 --> 00:24:07.363
But the Federal Modernization Workbook's
Book 07 chose Cloud PKI for these devices,

351
00:24:07.363 --> 00:24:12.233
and this would make the platform a second
issuer for a migrating population,

352
00:24:12.233 --> 00:24:15.403
which breaks Chapter 07's
first coexistence rule.

353
00:24:15.403 --> 00:24:19.276
It also adds a tenant-wide
consent, and Microsoft notes that

354
00:24:19.276 --> 00:24:22.991
revocation after a wipe depends
on each third party's API.

355
00:24:22.991 --> 00:24:24.565
Here's the second correction.

356
00:24:24.565 --> 00:24:31.453
Book 07 Chapter 04 says the platform
reads Cloud PKI's inventory for reporting.

357
00:24:31.453 --> 00:24:34.891
CyberArk documents no Cloud PKI import.

358
00:24:34.891 --> 00:24:40.084
What exists is Microsoft Graph's beta
Cloud PKI leaf-certificate report,

359
00:24:40.084 --> 00:24:42.940
and the platform's Discovery Import API.

360
00:24:42.940 --> 00:24:46.353
Joining them is a custom
job, on a beta API.

361
00:24:46.353 --> 00:24:48.685
Book 07 has been updated to say that,

362
00:24:48.685 --> 00:24:53.190
and that Intune's certificates
report remains the system of record.

363
